Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 09:41:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Hold every reviewer's verdict to a named check and keep
 the README live count

An independent review of 7b1e5acf found the record change faithful: all 74
round two rows equal the staged record and the three reviewers' own journal
outputs, all 114 carry proofs recompute, and no approval breaks a rule. It
raised two blocking findings, both repaired here.

1. The version three tests remove a forged row from its round, so the round
   check refused the record before the rule that every named reviewer judged
   an approved item ran, and removing that rule failed no named check.
   test_the_generator_refuses_an_approval_missing_one_named_reviewers_decision
   keeps the row in its round and drops one reviewer's decision. Mutant: with
   the check at build_host_catalogue_manifest.py _judged removed, the test
   fails; restored, it passes.
2. README.md said 114 items are in the deployed release. The live service
   serves 43 until a catalogue release of the 114 is published, so the README
   keeps 43. The homepage count stays 114 because its check holds it to the
   packaged manifest; that page should go live only with or after the release.

Also: test_the_generator_refuses_an_item_that_has_no_row_in_the_review_record
restores the check the round two recording brief asked for (an item with no
row at all is refused as review_does_not_cover_catalogue, also when named with
--include); removing the coverage check fails it with three errors. The
known-wrong case for the review sheet now plants each round's revision in its
own case, so a rule loosened to allow one round's revision still fails.

