he most common pattern. In a free text column the most common pattern covers 5 percent of the values, so the checker flags the other 95 percent. The share threshold prevents this. Below the threshold the correct answer is that the column has no dominant pattern.\n\n## What to record\n\n- The total, the dominant pattern, its share and the threshold.\n- Each flagged value with its position, its pattern, its confidence and its reason.\n- The statement that there is no dominant pattern, when that is the result.\n\n## Source\n\n- `src/loop_engine/code_nodes/field_recovery.py`: `detect_malformed`.\n- `src/loop_engine/code_nodes/text_conformance_operations.py`: `induce_pattern`.\n\nLicence: MIT. Compiled from revision 4be111f. The two modules depend only on each other and on the Python standard library.\n",
